<title>USA: GOLF-RAIN SHORTENS PGA QUALIFYING TOURNAMENT, 49 WIN U.S. CARDS. [CORRECTED 23:41 GMT]</title>
<headline>GOLF-RAIN SHORTENS PGA QUALIFYING TOURNAMENT, 49 WIN U.S. CARDS. [CORRECTED 23:41 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>GOLETA, California 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Forty nine players</p>
<p>earned their U.S. PGA Tour cards for the 1997 season Tuesday</p>
<p>based on results from the rain-shortened PGA Qualifying</p>
<p>Tournament.</p>
<p>As rain washed out the scheduled sixth round of play for a</p>
<p>second successive day, the tournament was reduced to 90 holes.</p>
<p>The top 40 scorers plus ties in the 110-man field (cut at 360)</p>
<p>through five rounds were granted membership.</p>
<p>Allen Doyle and Jimmy Johnston led the tournament with</p>
<p>eight-under-par totals of 352 over the La Purisima Golf Course</p>
<p>and Sandpiper Golf Course layouts that were employed.</p>
<p>Five international players won their U.S. tour cards -- (Corrects from four) Phil Tataurangi of New Zealand (355), Gabriel Hjerstedt of</p>
<p>Sweden (356), Hideki Kase of Japan (357), Rafael Alarcon of</p>
<p>Mexico (358) and Canadian Dave Barr (360).</p>
<p>Earned U.S. PGA Tour cards for 1997 (U.S. unless stated):</p>
<p>352 Allen Doyle 72 70 70 72 68, Jimmy Johnston 71 72 68 71 70</p>
<p>353 Doug Barron 70 72 71 71 69, Chip Sullivan 74 70 71 67 71</p>
<p>354 Jimmy Green 71 77 70 67 69, Tom Pernice Jr. 70 69 74 71</p>
